######## Transfer Learning
[tagline] "Reuse a pretrained network's features and retrain only the head."
[topicId] "transfer_learning"
[whatIsIt[0]] "Transfer learning reuses a network already trained on a large dataset and adapts it to a new task, instead of training from random initialization."
[whatIsIt[1]] "It works because early layers learn generic structure — edges, textures, syntax — that is not specific to the original labels. Replacing only the final head and training that on a few thousand examples routinely beats a from-scratch model trained on the same small dataset."
